# SUPPA2 Splicing Event Visualiser

## Overview

The **SUPPA2 Event Visualiser** provides a workflow for visualising alternative splicing events identified by SUPPA2, including:

- Skipped Exons (SE)
- Alternative 5′ Splice Sites (A5)
- Alternative 3′ Splice Sites (A3)
- Mutually Exclusive Exons (MX)
- Retained Introns (RI)
- Alternative First Exons (AF)
- Alternative Last Exons (AL)

The workflow was developed for visualising splicing events from long-read RNA-seq datasets. For reliable splicing analysis, transcript identification and quantification using **bambu** is recommended.

This repository assumes that SUPPA2 events have already been generated. Please refer to the SUPPA2 documentation for additional details.

## Generating SUPPA2 Input Files

```bash
python3.4 suppa.py generateEvents \
    -i <input-file.gtf> \
    -o <output-file> \
    -f ioe \
    -e <list-of-events>

python3.4 suppa.py psiPerEvent \
    --ioe-file <ioe-file> \
    --expression-file <expression-file> \
    -o <output-file>

python3.4 suppa.py diffSplice \
    --method empirical \
    --input <ioe-file> \
    --psi <Cond1.psi> <Cond2.psi> \
    --tpm <Cond1_expression-file> <Cond2_expression-file> \
    --area 1000 \
    --lower-bound 0.05 \
    -gc \
    -o <output-file>
```

Before running the visualisation script, SUPPA2 outputs generated for individual event types must be merged into combined files.

---

## Required Input Files

The visualisation workflow requires:

- `.ioe` file*
- PSI file for Condition 1*
- PSI file for Condition 2*
- delta PSI file*
- GTF file containing transcript annotations

\* Files generated separately for individual event types must be merged into a single combined file.

---

## Preparing Combined Files

### Combine PSI Files

```bash
for i in AF AL A5 A3 MX SE RI; do
    cat "$i/psi_cond1.psi" >> psi_cond1_combined.txt
    cat "$i/psi_cond2.psi" >> psi_cond2_combined.txt
done
```

### Combine delta PSI Files

```bash
for i in AF AL A5 A3 MX SE RI; do
    cat "$i/deltapsi_cond1_vs_cond2_dpsi.txt" >> combined_delta_psi_cond1_vs_cond2.txt
done
```

> **Note:** Modify filenames as required to match your SUPPA2 output files.

### Remove Duplicate Headers

After merging files, remove duplicated header lines generated during concatenation.

---

## Events of Interest File

Create a file containing one event ID per line.

Example (`events_of_interest.txt`):

```text
ENSG00000160323.19;AF:chr9:133414358:133414644-133423101:133422367:133422548-133423101:+
ENSG00000167525.16;AF:chr17:28704843-28710871:28711299:28704843-28711570:28711854:-
ENSG00000181450.18;AL:chr1:227654476-227677179:227677443:227654476-
.19_and_ENSG00000223262.1;A5:chr21:42288073-42288211:42288037-42288211:+
```

Replace the example entries with the events from your own dataset.

---

## Running the Pipeline

Edit the input file paths in:

```bash
run_splicing_visualisation.sh
```

Then execute:

```bash
bash run_splicing_visualisation.sh
```

Plots will be generated for all events listed in `events_of_interest.txt`.
The script requires all specified events to be present in every input file and will return an error if any event is missing.

